WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:04.440
Catelyn Stark: In the snow-capped Mountains
of the Moon, standing high above the rich

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:12.620
lands of the Vale, stands the Eyrie, a storied
and impregnable fortress said to have built

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:17.830
by the legendary Mountain Kings in the Age
of Heroes.

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:24.220
It is the stronghold of House Arryn, one of
the oldest noble families in Westeros.

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:34.590
Their sigil, a soaring white falcon over a
crescent moon; their words, "As High As Honor."

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:41.270
The Arryns are direct descendants of Andal
invaders, who sailed across the Narrow Sea

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:44.270
and came ashore at the Fingers.

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:50.910
According to legend, Ser Artys Arryn, known
as "the Winged Knight," soared through the

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:56.809
skies atop a giant falcon, landing on the
peak of the highest mountain, where he defeated

00:00:56.809 --> 00:01:36.869
the Griffin King 

00:01:36.869 --> 00:01:45.820
in battle.

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:49.640
It was the Andals' first great victory over
the First Men.

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:53.520
And SerArtys was duly rewarded.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:02:00.740
He was declared King of the Mountain and the
Vale, and the region renamed "the Vale of

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:01.820
Arryn."

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:05.979
Thousands of years later, Aegon the Conqueror
arrived in Westeros.

00:02:05.979 --> 00:02:10.970
House Arryn bent the knee to Aegon and his
dragons and were allowed to maintain their

00:02:10.970 --> 00:02:16.620
control of the region as Lords Paramount of
the Vale and Wardens of the East.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:21.250
Petyr Baelish: The Vale of Arryn was the last
of the great kingdoms left.

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:27.660
Old and proud, House Arryn did what they always
did in times of strife: they shut the Bloody

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:30.290
Gate, sealing off the Vale.

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:36.459
Then, the Queen Regent Sharra of House Arryn
retreated with her son, the boy-king Ronnel,

00:02:36.459 --> 00:02:40.800
into the Eyrie, their family's impregnable
fortress.

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:46.070
From the top of their mountain, they could
look down on Westeros far below, its problems

00:02:46.070 --> 00:02:48.879
hidden beneath the clouds.

00:02:48.879 --> 00:02:53.180
But one day, Queen Sharra entered the outer
courtyard to find her young son sitting on

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:58.260
the knee of Visenya Targaryen and ogling her
dragon, Vhagar, beside her.

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:03.260
Just as he asked for another cake at dinner,
little King Ronnel asked his mother if he

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:06.480
could ride on the nice lady's dragon.

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:08.790
Visenya smiled at Sharra.

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:13.299
So, Sharra imagined, did Vhagar.

00:03:13.299 --> 00:03:18.480
Remembering her manners, Sharra asked if she
could have Visenya brought some wine or food,

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:21.739
she must be tired after such a long flight.

00:03:21.739 --> 00:03:23.709
But Visenya demurred.

00:03:23.709 --> 00:03:28.090
Bored with his mother's pleasantries, Ronnel
demanded an answer.

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:29.450
Poor boy.

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:33.110
He didn't even understand the question.

00:03:33.110 --> 00:03:39.041
Sharra hesitated for a moment, then asked
Visenya, as a mother, if it was safe for the

00:03:39.041 --> 00:03:40.189
boy.

00:03:40.189 --> 00:03:42.489
Visenya assured her it was.

00:03:42.489 --> 00:03:45.500
What choice did Sharra have?

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:51.970
Whilst her son circled the castle, she collected
his little ringlet, her own regent's coronet,

00:03:51.970 --> 00:03:57.060
and the ancient Falcon Crown of Mountain and
Vale, which the Arryns had worn for thousands

00:03:57.060 --> 00:03:59.000
of years.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:03.370
Ronnel had taken to the sky as a king, but
he landed as a lordling.

00:04:03.370 --> 00:04:08.391
Perhaps he considered his ancient rights a
fair trade for a few minutes of flight, as

00:04:08.391 --> 00:04:10.500
a little boy would.

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:16.800
More likely, he didn't even notice the three
crowns at Visenya's feet or recognize the

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:19.450
swords of his garrison beside them.

00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:25.990
Catelyn Stark: Over the centuries, the House
Arryn remained loyal to the Targaryen dynasty.

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:34.080
Until Lord Jon Arryn joined with Houses Baratheon
and Stark in rebellion against Mad King Aerys.

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:39.410
Petyr Baelish: No army in the Seven Kingdoms
can match the pride and chivalry of the Knights

00:04:39.410 --> 00:04:40.410
of the Vale.

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:45.210
After all, they were the first true knights
in Westeros.

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:51.199
The Knights of the Vale were originally the
knights of Andalos, an eastern nation whose

00:04:51.199 --> 00:04:55.350
people invaded Westeros thousands of years
ago.

00:04:55.350 --> 00:05:00.460
From the sea, the Vale seemed to the Andals
an ideal new home.

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:06.070
A wide, fertile valley isolated from the rest
of Westeros and its kingdoms by a great mountain

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:07.160
range.

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:14.199
The First Men who held it, moreover, were
sparse and divided and waded into battle with

00:05:14.199 --> 00:05:19.790
bronze axes and armor that couldn't match
Andal horses and steel.

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:24.990
But what the First Men lacked in weaponry
they made up for in ferocity.

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:32.100
Finally uniting behind King Robar Royce, the
First Men smashed the Andals in battle after

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:37.139
battle, reclaiming the Vale and pushing the
invaders back to the sea from whence they'd

00:05:37.139 --> 00:05:38.530
come.

00:05:38.530 --> 00:05:44.250
Learning from the First Men, the remaining
Andals united behind a leader of their own.

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:50.170
Not a king or a lord, but a knight who'd been
born in the Vale and knew it as well as the

00:05:50.170 --> 00:05:51.170
First Men.

00:05:51.170 --> 00:05:55.790
Ser Artys Arryn, known as the Falcon Knight.

00:05:55.790 --> 00:06:01.650
The armies of the First Men and the Andals
met beneath the Giant's Lance to decide the

00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:03.849
fate of the Vale.

00:06:03.849 --> 00:06:09.300
SerArtys had many more mounted knights than
the First Men, who preferred to fight on foot.

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:14.520
But the First Men had seized the high ground,
digging trenches in front of their ranks and

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:18.770
lining them with sharpened stakes smeared
with offal and excrement.

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:25.500
Six times the Andal knights charged, and six
times the First Men threw them back.

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:31.960
But on the seventh, a fearsome Andal warrior
broke through the ranks of the First Men,

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:35.110
and the Andals rushed through the gap.

00:06:35.110 --> 00:06:40.260
If King Robar had been wiser, he would have
retreated and saved his army for another day.

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:44.919
Then again, if he'd been wise at all, he'd
never have risked his army of foot soldiers

00:06:44.919 --> 00:06:47.160
against mounted knights in the first place.

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:53.730
When King Robar saw the falcon helm of SerArtys
across the field, he wagered that the Andals

00:06:53.730 --> 00:06:59.349
would break if they lost their leader and
rode hard for the Falcon Knight.

00:06:59.349 --> 00:07:04.910
The singers paint a pretty picture of the
battle—the king in flashing bronze armor,

00:07:04.910 --> 00:07:08.169
the knight in silvered steel.

00:07:08.169 --> 00:07:12.110
But the duel lasted no longer than a verse
of the songs.

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:17.470
For King Robar had taken a Valyrian sword
off a dead Andal lord, and it sheared through

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:21.870
SerArtys' helm much like a bird's wing through
the air.

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:27.759
As the Falcon Knight tumbled to Earth, King
Robar thought he'd won his desperate gamble.

00:07:27.759 --> 00:07:31.229
Then he heard the trumpets behind him.

00:07:31.229 --> 00:07:39.289
When he turned, he saw 500 fresh Andal knights
pouring down the Giant's Lance, and the man

00:07:39.289 --> 00:07:42.810
at its head was also the man at Robar's feet.

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:50.180
For SerArtys, unique in that age, or indeed
any age, esteemed cunning even more than martial

00:07:50.180 --> 00:07:56.310
strength and had clad one of his knights in
his spare suit of armor, leaving him to die

00:07:56.310 --> 00:08:04.129
at Robar's hand while SerArtys took his best
horsemen up a goat track he knew from childhood.

00:08:04.129 --> 00:08:09.770
The charge of the Andal knights broke the
last great army of the First Men, who would

00:08:09.770 --> 00:08:13.819
never again threaten the new Knights of the
Vale.

00:08:13.819 --> 00:08:18.190
Some of the defeated would even join their
ranks in the years to come, but many more

00:08:18.190 --> 00:08:22.580
fled to the mountains, choosing savagery over
submission.

00:08:22.580 --> 00:08:28.569
Ever since, the Knights of the Vale enjoyed
an exclusive position in Westeros.

00:08:28.569 --> 00:08:32.950
They could sally forth from the Vale at will,
knowing that if battle went against them,

00:08:32.950 --> 00:08:37.289
they could retreat through the Bloody Gate
where no army could follow.

00:08:37.289 --> 00:08:40.530
Until the dragons changed the game.

00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:45.440
When Aegon the Conqueror landed in Westeros,
the Queen Regent of the Vale shut the Bloody

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:50.640
Gate against the Targaryens and massed the
Knights of the Vale behind it to lock it.

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:56.519
But Visenya simply flew her dragon to a balcony
of the Eyrie, where the boy king was playing

00:08:56.519 --> 00:09:01.579
and gave the boy a ride around the castle
in return for his mother's submission.

00:09:01.579 --> 00:09:08.490
With the Conquest, no more could the Knights
of the Vale hide behind their mountains, nor,

00:09:08.490 --> 00:09:11.720
they soon discovered, did they need to.

00:09:11.720 --> 00:09:16.260
For thousands of years, the other kingdoms
had warred and treated to balance each other's

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:17.260
might.

00:09:17.260 --> 00:09:20.180
whilst the Vale kept to itself.

00:09:20.180 --> 00:09:26.140
None realized what power the Vale could have
until Jon Arryn defied the Iron Throne, refusing

00:09:26.140 --> 00:09:29.630
to surrender Ned Stark and Robert Baratheon
to the Mad King.

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:35.079
The North, the Riverlands, and the Stormlands
couldn't have beaten the other three kingdoms

00:09:35.079 --> 00:09:36.079
be themselves.

00:09:36.079 --> 00:09:40.029
But the Knights of the Vale rode with them.

00:09:40.029 --> 00:09:45.720
After all, the Vale's isolation does breed
an abundance of honor and pious bleating,

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:49.110
which governs their decisions instead of foresight.

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:54.160
Like a blind man who can only guess where
his horse is taking him, I doubt Jon Arryn

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:58.820
had even prepared for civil war when he raised
his banners instead of handing over his young

00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:02.440
wards, Ned Stark and Robert Baratheon, to
the Mad King.

00:10:02.440 --> 00:10:05.660
Honor demanded, and Lord Arryn obeyed.

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:10.709
He'd have done the same if the boys hadn't
been the lords of two Great Houses, who could

00:10:10.709 --> 00:10:13.330
field mighty armies of their own.

00:10:13.330 --> 00:10:15.980
But perhaps I give him too little credit.

00:10:15.980 --> 00:10:22.780
After all, if the war went against them, only
Lord Arryn had a nice impregnable castle to

00:10:22.780 --> 00:10:28.399
retreat into; and he was wise enough to take
poor Lysa Tully into his bed to win the Riverlands

00:10:28.399 --> 00:10:30.010
as allies.

00:10:30.010 --> 00:10:33.209
Jon Arryn won, then Jon Arryn died.

00:10:33.209 --> 00:10:34.209
Impregnable.

00:10:34.209 --> 00:10:37.880
That's how the Vale sees itself.

00:10:37.880 --> 00:10:40.430
Shielded from Westeros by its mountains.

00:10:40.430 --> 00:10:46.660
They call the entrance to their lands the
Bloody Gate because, during the Age of Heroes,

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:50.580
a dozen armies supposedly smashed themselves
against it.

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:52.899
Except the Vale has been conquered.

00:10:52.899 --> 00:10:58.160
Those vaunted mountains didn't stop the Andals
who came by the eastern sea.

00:10:58.160 --> 00:11:02.339
The people of the Vale say that Ser Artys
Arryn, the Andal general, flew on the back

00:11:02.339 --> 00:11:08.070
of a giant falcon and slew the Griffin King
on top of the tallest mountain.

00:11:08.070 --> 00:11:13.660
During Aegon's conquest, one of his sisters
did the same, flying a dragon over the Bloody

00:11:13.660 --> 00:11:16.550
Gate and up to the Eyrie, the Arryn stronghold.

00:11:16.550 --> 00:11:48.899
And the Arryn boy king yielded the Vale in
return for a ride on 

00:11:48.899 --> 00:11:50.110
the beast.

